WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.730
Everyone has a weak spot, and there's bound
to be a film out there that pushes one or

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.130
two of your buttons.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.470
These movies, on the other hand, push all
of them.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.200
They aren't just hard to watch.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.040
They're deeply disturbing on almost every
level, and some of them are downright vile.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.379
In fact, many people couldn't even finish
them, and for good reason.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.340
Hold on, because these are some of the most
disturbing movies ever made.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.340
Veronica

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.890
Netflix's quick ascent to the top of the entertainment
industry goes hand-in-hand with the rise of

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.890
binge-watching.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.160
In fact, the company seems dedicated to trying
its best to make sure that you never, ever

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.180
turn off your television.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.250
That's what makes Veronica so surprising.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.050
In March 2018, this Spanish-language horror
film made headlines because people were so

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.949
scared that they couldn't make it through
the entire thing, and Netflix couldn't be

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:44.949
happier.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:47.660
Plot-wise, Veronica doesn't break any new
ground.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.340
The title character misses her deceased father,
and her friend wants to talk to a deceased

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.739
boyfriend, and so the girls use a Ouija board
and a solar eclipse to summon their spirits.

00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:01.129
As tends to happen when Ouija boards are involved,
things don't go according to plan.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:02.390
You know what to expect.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.809
Or, at least, you think you do.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:08.700
Veronica succeeds where other films fall short
through a mixture of real-life terror and

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.310
pitch-perfect filmmaking.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.890
It knows how to push all the right buttons,
and that elevates a standard horror flick

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.780
to what some people are calling the "scariest
movie ever."

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.850
After watching Veronica, some viewers are
plagued by nightmares for days.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.300
Others can only go to sleep with the lights
on after watching.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.400
And those are just the people who finished
the movie.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:37.909
Many don't make it that far.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:39.050
Life is short, after all.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.160
Why spend the rest of it cowering in fear?

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.160
Teeth

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.030
Of course, Veronica isn't the only disturbing
movie on Netflix that people keep bailing

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.030
on.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.869
In Veronica's aftermath, the streaming service
reached out to Forbes and provided a list

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:56.490
of ten movies that are so scary, people just
won't watch them until the end.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.520
Many of the entries on the list make sense.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.750
The Human Centipede 2: Full Sequence?

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.009
So gross that it was banned in Britain and
in Australia.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:08.530
And if the violence in 2016's Cabin Fever
doesn't get you, the rest of the production

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.330
probably will: it has a shockingly low rating
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.660
And yet, even among these shockers, Teeth
stands out.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.000
In the film, the main character is Dawn O'Keefe,
a Christian abstinence advocate who suffers

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.830
from a condition that or, to put it as mildly
as possible, has teeth where she shouldn't

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.070
have teeth.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.970
As such, many of Teeth's scenes aren't just
uncomfortable.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.910
They're intentionally squirm-inducing, especially
for the guys in the audience.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:36.080
It's no wonder so few viewers last until the
credits roll.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.260
Mother!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.800
Darren Aronofsky's mother! isn't a traditional
horror movie.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.030
It doesn't have any monsters or supernatural
threats, but that doesn't make the film any

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.030
less troubling.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.590
Love it or hate it, mother! is successfully
disturbing, thanks largely to the brutal and

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.850
relentless abuse heaped on Jennifer Lawrence's
character.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.720
Taken all together, it's kind of a lot.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.160
Too much, in fact.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.890
Some critics found mother!'s graphic depictions
supremely distasteful.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.060
Audiences agreed.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.670
People flocked to the exits during mother!'s
theatrical screenings, and we can't say we

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.480
blame 'em.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.480
Raw

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.060
Maybe you didn't complete a film because you
decided to turn it off.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.790
Maybe you're simply too grossed out to stay
in the theater.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.280
Sometimes, however, you don't have a choice.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.870
People didn't just walk out of Raw.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.800
They found the movie so disturbing that they
passed out in the theater.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.140
Try finishing a movie while you're unconscious.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:28.170
As far as Raw is concerned, it only takes
a single scene to get everyone's stomachs

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.170
heaving.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:33.580
When Raw begins, veterinary student Justine
is a lifelong vegetarian, but she's forced

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.110
to consume meat as part of a hazing ritual.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.520
As a result, she's consumed by a very specific
hunger.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.250
A hamburger doesn't do the trick.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.180
Neither does raw chicken.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.640
It's only after Justine's sister accidentally
cuts off her own finger and passes out that

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.210
Justine finds the answer.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:53.280
Justine picks up the severed appendage and...you
get the idea.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.340
For a couple of viewers at the Toronto International
Film Festival, that was enough.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.370
At least two people passed out, forcing the
festival to call an ambulance.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.180
Others fled to prevent vomiting.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.480
And that's just the beginning, too, Justine's
cravings don't end with just a finger, and

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.260
it's probably best for everyone that the more
sensitive members of the audience didn't stick

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.090
around to see just how depraved things get.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.090
A Serbian Film

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.720
Even if you've got an unnaturally high tolerance
for grotesque scenes in movies, you've probably

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.250
got some kind of limit.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.870
Chances are, A Serbian Film will find it,
and then blow right past it.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:29.120
Of course, A Serbian Film isn't just shocking
for shock's sake.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.370
It's got social and political messages.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.970
That's what the director says, anyway.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.520
He told Electric Sheep Magazine:

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:39.350
"It's a struggle against all the corrupt authorities
that govern our lives for their own purposes."

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.310
When it comes to Serbia specifically, the
director said the movie represents a metaphor

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.310
for

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:48.970
"The monolithic power of leaders who hypnotize
you to do things you don't want to do."

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.280
Whether it's successful is up for debate.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.100
What we do know is that A Serbian Film is
intensely disturbing.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.000
Even some employees at the distribution company
responsible for its U.S. release couldn't

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.000
finish it.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.400
Unless you're desensitized to, well, everything,
there's no reason to think that you'll do

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.510
any better.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.030
Caligula

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.060
According to legend, the Roman emperor Caligula
wasn't a nice guy, and the movie Caligula

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.750
is as depraved as its subject matter.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.350
There's also just way too much of it.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.100
With a runtime that borders on three hours,
Caligula requires a major time investment,

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.070
and all of that debauchery gets exhausting
fast.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:27.660
Even acclaimed film critic Roger Ebert couldn't
sit through it, saying: "Disgusted and unspeakably

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.080
depressed, I walked out of the film after
two hours of its 170-minute length."

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.550
The Great Ecstasy of Robert Carmichael

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:38.780
You could watch The Great Ecstasy of Robert
Carmichael all the way through, but why?

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.710
By all accounts, the film is thoroughly unpleasant.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.390
According to Variety, a few of its scenes,
quote, "make A Clockwork Orange look like

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.130
a Britney Spears video."

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:50.920
When the film screened at Cannes, one scene
prompted a mass walkout.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.860
Given that one critic called The Great Ecstasy
of Robert Carmichael's climax "a sequence

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:59.030
excruciating beyond any in memory," we're
going to bet that the Cannes showing wasn't

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.660
the only time everyone bailed.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.560
Not that the rest of The Great Ecstasy of
Robert Carmichael is particularly easy to

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.740
watch, of course.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:10.120
By the time Robert becomes an ecstasy dealer,
he's more or less beyond redemption...and

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.050
the audience is more or less done with it
all.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.490
Hereditary

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.860
In Hereditary, Toni Collette plays an artist,
Annie, who just lost her borderline-abusive

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.140
mother to cancer.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:24.510
Meanwhile, her relationships with her husband,
her son, and her daughter are slowly deteriorating.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:27.340
That's enough to make Hereditary uncomfortable
from the start.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:30.430
When the scares start dropping, it becomes
unbearable.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:34.490
Writer-director Ari Aster describes his critically
acclaimed haunted house film as a personal

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.490
project, saying,

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.490
"I had gone through some stuff with my family.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:40.580
I took my sickness and now put it inside all
of you."

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:45.180
Aster didn't elaborate further, but whatever
the issue was, it must've been messed up.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.141
Hereditary isn't just the strongest debut
from a horror director since Get Out, it's

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:52.919
one of the most terrifying films to come along
in years, if you can manage to sit through

00:06:52.919 --> 00:06:53.960
the whole thing.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.180
Not everyone can.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:59.610
While Hereditary received rave reviews when
it screened at Sundance, it was also scary

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.040
enough to drive many viewers from the theater.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:05.120
Even people who stayed for the whole thing
didn't really want to.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.320
By all accounts, the film isn't unsettling
because of its jump scares; It's hard to watch

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.020
because the characters' pain is so real.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.280
Meet the Feebles

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.800
If you're bored, try this: invite some friends
over, make sure they're relaxed, and then

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.620
put on Meet the Feebles.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.840
Don't tell them what's coming.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:25.139
Don't reveal that what starts as a low-budget
Muppet knockoff quickly transforms into something

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:26.580
much, much worse.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.260
Let your buddies discover that for themselves,
and see how long it takes before you don't

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.570
have any friends left.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:35.889
Anyone who grew up with the Muppets will either
find Meet the Feebles darkly hilarious or

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:37.620
deeply disturbing.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.310
Watching off-brand versions of Jim Henson's
classic characters dropped into the seedy

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.230
underbelly of a crime-ridden city is nearly
unbearable.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:48.370
Oh, and did we mention that Meet the Feebles
was directed by Peter Jackson, the man who

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.260
brought Middle-earth to the big screen?

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.639
Yup, that's right.

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:55.000
At some point, someone saw Meet the Feebles
and thought Peter Jackson should be given

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.040
nearly $300 million dollars and the freedom
to make a few of the most ambitious films

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.040
of all time.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.690
Sure, Meet the Feebles may be too disturbing
for many viewers to finish, but for Peter

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.620
Jackson, it worked out very well indeed.

